leffler@physics.ubc.ca (Steve Leffler ) writes:

>   One thing about hack that I'm not clear on is the aggravate monster
>intrinsic.  I seem to see it come up a lot when I die and view my intrinsics.
>Besides eating your dog or wearing a ring of aggravate monster, how do you
>get this intrinsic?  What exactly does it do? I know it makes the monster
>problem worse somehow, but how?  Most importantly, once you've got it, is there
>any way of getting rid of it?

>				     ---Steven Leffler
>					leffler@physics.ubc.ca

You can get it in several ways.                                    
But that would be a spoiler....
First, never eat a dog or cat corpse.  Even if it's not your pet's.  There
is also a ring of aggravate monster, so be careful not to wear rings you
havn't ID'd yet.  A good rule of thumb is to never wear a cursed ring until
you've identified it.

I think you can also get it by angering your God.  For instance, don't do
things like killing shopkeepers or whacking your pet if you are lawful.

What it does is this:  Monsters are automatically drawn towards you.  You
may have noticed that some monsters are standing still when you enter a
room, like nymphs or leprechans, or rooms full of killer bees, et al.
They're sleeping.  If you have aggrevate monster they'll come chasing
after you.  

There are a couple of ways to get rid of it, but only one that's really
very plausible.  You need to gain the "stealth" intrinsic.  This can be
obtained with a ring, or certain elvin clothing.  Stealth cancels out any
aggravate monster intrinsic you may have, and also gives you some other
benefits - like taking on a whole army of sleeping monsters one by one
instead of waking them all up the first time you attack one of them.

Good luck, and quit eating those puppies.

